            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=hossman&avatarId=21247",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=hossman&avatarId=21247",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=hossman&avatarId=21247",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=hossman&avatarId=21247"
            },
            "displayName": "Chris M. Hostetter",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/Phoenix"
          },
          "body": "since SegmentInfos is final, and all of it's methods are (at best) package protected i don't think it's a big risk to make it private again (without requiring a bump to lucene-3.0.0)\n\nI'm not sure if re-privatizing this class really neccessitates a 2.1.1 release ... it doesn't cause any bugs, and it does't really give people very much rope to hang themselves with unless they are going out of their way to put stuff in the org.apache.lucene.index package.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=hossman",
            "name": "hossman",
            "key": "hossman",
            "avatarUrls": {
